00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:34.960
So let's talk a little bit
about our own, you know,

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.210
like personal encounters

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:39.227
with our very first knowledge of Myanmar

00:12:39.227 --> 00:12:42.704
and what's happening in the country.

00:12:42.704 --> 00:12:43.537
In 2021, I participated in
an art writing symposium

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:52.580
that contains a lot of like
curators and art labors

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.210
and artists across Southeast Asia.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:58.257
And we got together in
this specific program

00:12:58.257 --> 00:13:00.430
called Term and Condition

00:13:01.608 --> 00:13:03.420
or reading and publishing
in Southeast Asia

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:08.420
organized by a certified
now and (indistinct)

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:12.927
under the organization (indistinct).

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:18.070
So in this very specific
program, we talk a lot about,

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:21.675
you know, like the state
of culture production

00:13:21.675 --> 00:13:22.920
in contemporary.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:25.230
So Asian as well, a lot of the history

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:30.160
that underline this very
process of development.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.440
And as I had a talk with a specific,

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:37.250
this very specific like Burmese scholar

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:41.840
who just got back from
getting her degree in the US,

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.567
she got back right back to Myanmar

00:13:43.567 --> 00:13:46.820
and started working there as a teacher

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:51.820
and also in parallel with
raising fund for the resistance,

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:56.070
which is something very powerful.

00:13:56.070 --> 00:14:00.570
I had not known before,
because a lot of the people

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:03.710
who join the revolution are
actually people at my age,

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:08.710
and I can just not faith
them, how that very audacity

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:12.500
and a belief in something
that is judicious

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:17.500
for by a collective democracy
would be that powerful

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:23.500
to mobilize such a
massive number of people.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:26.360
And especially, again,
those are people at my age,

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.920
the youngsters are putting
themselves out there

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:33.040
and facing direct and seeing the brutality

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:36.340
committed on daily basis.

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:38.260
So I decide that's the moment for me

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:43.120
to get to know a lot more about
what's happening in Myanmar.

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:46.740
And most of my information
comes from Instagram

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.500
because we are like gen z people, right?

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:50.619
So we do a lot of Instagrams,

00:14:50.619 --> 00:14:54.280
and it's very interesting to
see that a lot of these reports

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:56.400
from independent journalists

00:14:56.400 --> 00:15:01.400
often come from Instagram
accounts that are often private

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:04.620
so that you can see the
contents with the censorship.

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:09.620
And those become my main
sources of information

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:12.715
to keep me updated about situation

00:15:12.715 --> 00:15:17.410
and like which regions of Myanmar
is turning into a war zone

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.313
and stuff like that.

00:15:20.315 --> 00:15:24.820
And in light of the
Ukraine Russia conflict

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.550
that is happening recently,

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:27.697
you know, the news of the Myanmar,

00:15:27.697 --> 00:15:30.310
and especially there's
one specific article

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:33.910
about us and being in prison

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:36.280
or being charged with
three years in prisons,

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:37.980
it just made it to the news

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:40.610
for around like three
days before sliding back

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:45.530
into the virtual archive of the internet,

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:48.350
which is something that I
cannot really understand

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:50.820
because like the level
of brutarian balance

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:54.761
is just beyond our understanding,

00:15:54.761 --> 00:15:58.290
especially in the contact
with 21st century.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:00.280
So we decided to...

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:05.280
This is the moment when we
bring all of this to the right.

