So this was already
oppression in Mandalay.

00:35:24.540 --> 00:35:27.100
And then early May,

00:35:27.100 --> 00:35:30.400
we got the last picture
from our journalist in Tamwe

00:35:32.578 --> 00:35:35.040
where it just went very violent.

00:35:35.040 --> 00:35:37.490
So it went for the flash strike.

00:35:37.490 --> 00:35:41.930
So 15 people went away and
even then even on this day,

00:35:41.930 --> 00:35:43.345
people got arrested.

00:35:43.345 --> 00:35:45.760
So it got very dangerous.

00:35:45.760 --> 00:35:48.193
So we switch to first,

00:35:51.820 --> 00:35:56.520
we collaborate with the NGO
human rights in the picture

00:35:56.520 --> 00:35:59.470
we based in the Netherlands
and for decades,

00:35:59.470 --> 00:36:03.400
they are helping filmmakers in countries

00:36:03.400 --> 00:36:05.620
where you have a huge political shock

00:36:05.620 --> 00:36:07.700
where people cannot walk anymore.

00:36:07.700 --> 00:36:11.480
And then to help them save their footage,

00:36:11.480 --> 00:36:14.316
to help them do something with it edit

00:36:14.316 --> 00:36:17.720
and give an audience to the movies.

00:36:17.720 --> 00:36:21.193
So we did the photo part and we created,

00:36:23.180 --> 00:36:28.180
sorry, visual rebellion you know.

00:36:29.380 --> 00:36:33.990
So this is collaboration

00:36:33.990 --> 00:36:37.320
between our collective
of photo journalists

00:36:37.320 --> 00:36:40.160
and this organization
who help film making.

00:36:40.160 --> 00:36:44.050
So the Major Reuben who is the founder.

00:36:44.050 --> 00:36:48.440
She helps put on this filmmaker

00:36:48.440 --> 00:36:53.090
that we will keep his name
anonymous to make his documentary

00:36:54.870 --> 00:36:59.140
because for months he films
in Yangon in Shan state,

00:36:59.140 --> 00:37:01.700
in Karen state and then
finally came to Thailand

00:37:01.700 --> 00:37:03.880
and now he's safe in another country,

00:37:03.880 --> 00:37:08.880
but we combine him all the way
so he can finish his movie.

00:37:09.750 --> 00:37:13.520
And so this is the website.

00:37:13.520 --> 00:37:16.360
And so the second thing
we decide to switch

00:37:16.360 --> 00:37:19.530
is that because we cannot
send people in the streets

00:37:19.530 --> 00:37:20.437
to cover street protest anymore,

00:37:20.437 --> 00:37:25.370
because it's so unsafe,
we switch to research.

00:37:25.370 --> 00:37:28.290
So as you know, most
international organization

00:37:28.290 --> 00:37:30.280
cannot send their people inside Myanmar

00:37:30.280 --> 00:37:32.720
to get information on the ground.

00:37:32.720 --> 00:37:34.330
The think tank cannot work.

00:37:34.330 --> 00:37:37.099
Most of the foreign staff
have been pulled out,

00:37:37.099 --> 00:37:41.900
and then you had all this
budget opportunities.

00:37:41.900 --> 00:37:44.290
This need to know what was happening.

00:37:44.290 --> 00:37:45.970
And we said, we can fulfill this need

00:37:45.970 --> 00:37:49.892
because we have trained
local media workers

00:37:49.892 --> 00:37:51.590
across the country.

00:37:51.590 --> 00:37:53.430
And we started doing research.

00:37:53.430 --> 00:37:57.259
So collaborating with Researcher Republic,

00:37:57.259 --> 00:38:01.136
which is a think tank that
was created 10 years ago

00:38:01.136 --> 00:38:06.136
in Myanmar and they provide
confidential reports.

00:38:09.500 --> 00:38:11.350
And then we publish with them

00:38:13.620 --> 00:38:17.363
a report about cyber security
in Post-Coup Myanmar.

00:38:18.510 --> 00:38:21.090
And then it's long report.

00:38:21.090 --> 00:38:23.480
You can see I will not open
them, it's 50 page each,

00:38:23.480 --> 00:38:27.450
but the idea was to
teach young journalists

00:38:27.450 --> 00:38:28.950
to work with young researcher,

00:38:28.950 --> 00:38:33.220
and then to get a comprehensive
idea of the situation

00:38:33.220 --> 00:38:36.750
that were both compelling in
a telling a journalistic way,

00:38:36.750 --> 00:38:39.390
but also with the academic context.

00:38:40.573 --> 00:38:44.023
So this one was about all
the economic difficulties

00:38:46.670 --> 00:38:48.410
in the country and how people are coping,

00:38:48.410 --> 00:38:50.130
how people are resisting.

00:38:50.130 --> 00:38:53.443
Our last one publish is about the world

00:38:53.443 --> 00:38:55.230
that is being built at the moment,

00:38:55.230 --> 00:38:57.770
between China and Myanmar.

00:38:57.770 --> 00:39:01.020
And so we choose topics
where we have people,

00:39:01.020 --> 00:39:04.540
but that are out of international
interest, of course,

00:39:04.540 --> 00:39:08.910
so the next one will be about the pipeline

00:39:08.910 --> 00:39:10.740
and what's something along the pipeline

00:39:10.740 --> 00:39:13.647
from our time to come in.

00:39:13.647 --> 00:39:18.647
And then we have one on the
situation of women in IDP camps

00:39:19.570 --> 00:39:22.690
millions of people, one
of displaced by the war

00:39:22.690 --> 00:39:24.909
and was a situation for them.

00:39:24.909 --> 00:39:29.909
And we also do, but this, all
of this is we provide content,

00:39:31.840 --> 00:39:35.292
but it's a school, it's to
continue the pedagogical,

00:39:35.292 --> 00:39:38.440
the training that was interrupted

00:39:38.440 --> 00:39:39.840
because of COVID of the coup,
because this is experience

00:39:41.530 --> 00:39:43.570
they would've learned by themselves,

00:39:43.570 --> 00:39:44.930
but now it's not possible.

00:39:44.930 --> 00:39:49.930
So we continue this journalism
school we do by learning.

00:39:49.930 --> 00:39:53.500
So they get a lot of time
to three, four months

00:39:53.500 --> 00:39:54.983
to work on a long future.

00:39:56.523 --> 00:39:57.570
And at the same time,

00:39:57.570 --> 00:40:01.290
we are doing a lot of work on the side.

00:40:01.290 --> 00:40:05.620
So we have English lesson
online every evening

00:40:05.620 --> 00:40:10.450
to be most opportunities to learn more.

00:40:10.450 --> 00:40:15.450
And for the people, what
to flee to Thailand,

00:40:15.720 --> 00:40:19.863
we help them logistically
we organize workshop here.

00:40:20.773 --> 00:40:25.773
And so the idea is to
provide all opportunities

00:40:27.630 --> 00:40:30.120
they should have to continue

00:40:30.120 --> 00:40:32.360
and to have a future as journalists,

00:40:32.360 --> 00:40:34.780
as academics at the same time

00:40:34.780 --> 00:40:39.270
that we provide very
localized verified content.

00:40:40.176 --> 00:40:45.110
And what we want to do is
actually to have Thai journalists

00:40:45.110 --> 00:40:47.450
and Burmese journalists working together,

00:40:47.450 --> 00:40:49.940
because most of Burmese people,

00:40:49.940 --> 00:40:52.640
when they can flee to Thailand.

00:40:52.640 --> 00:40:56.349
So you have lost of the media now here,

00:40:56.349 --> 00:40:59.800
and we're still working
with the sources in Myanmar,

00:40:59.800 --> 00:41:01.243
but we need support.

00:41:01.243 --> 00:41:03.170
A lot of them are in (indistinct) paper.

00:41:03.170 --> 00:41:06.711
So we also help with
this getting scholarship,

00:41:06.711 --> 00:41:11.711
getting them to university,
getting some paper.

00:41:14.436 --> 00:41:19.220
And this is why I have
also invited in the talk,

00:41:19.220 --> 00:41:20.220
my two colleagues.

00:41:20.220 --> 00:41:24.090
So we have Keyo who's a Thai journalist

00:41:24.090 --> 00:41:28.600
who was covering before for
Thai Media Myanmar issues.

00:41:28.600 --> 00:41:32.348
And then we have Nicole who
is basically the profounder

00:41:32.348 --> 00:41:35.590
of the collective because
he contacted me first.

00:41:35.590 --> 00:41:37.860
And is the journalist from Yangon,

00:41:37.860 --> 00:41:42.860
and is the author of this report.

00:41:44.320 --> 00:41:48.006
So we research cyber
security for four months

00:41:48.006 --> 00:41:50.107
and we published this

00:41:50.107 --> 00:41:52.710
and he is also the author of short movie.

00:41:52.710 --> 00:41:54.310
So if you allow me,

00:41:54.310 --> 00:41:56.510
I would like to show
you a short documentary

00:41:57.780 --> 00:42:02.780
that was done by him on this,
because we talk on signal

00:42:03.650 --> 00:42:05.020
and all his audio.

00:42:05.020 --> 00:42:07.634
I get all his stories by audio now.

00:42:07.634 --> 00:42:10.970
So this is one, this is his
experience from the ground.

00:42:10.970 --> 00:42:13.350
So we do photo research video

00:42:14.450 --> 00:42:18.950
why empowering people in
the professional life.

00:42:18.950 --> 00:42:21.676
So this is one movie and
we have six like this,

00:42:21.676 --> 00:42:24.093
and then I will pass to Keyo.

00:42:33.002 --> 00:42:35.447
(protestors ranting)

00:42:35.447 --> 00:42:37.600
- [Keyo] Sorry for my late reply

00:42:37.600 --> 00:42:42.600
As you know, it was
not easy to communicate

00:42:43.263 --> 00:42:46.180
because this situation is not good.

00:42:50.070 --> 00:42:51.050
It was two weeks ago

00:42:51.050 --> 00:42:55.570
and now so many people got hurt by a bomb.

00:42:55.570 --> 00:42:59.417
Every night two to three
bomb explode in the city.

00:43:04.350 --> 00:43:09.323
I mean I'm okay at least I was alive.

00:43:16.170 --> 00:43:17.587
I mean, I'm okay.

00:43:19.490 --> 00:43:23.223
I don't know how long we
will have this situation.

00:43:27.840 --> 00:43:32.840
Every day, I am thinking about my future.

00:43:37.200 --> 00:43:38.533
How long it will take?

00:43:40.707 --> 00:43:43.800
And how long we have to wait

00:43:45.980 --> 00:43:50.460
to end this?

00:43:50.460 --> 00:43:53.160
Sometimes I was lose my ambition.

00:44:01.040 --> 00:44:02.533
Sometimes I was depressed.

00:44:04.730 --> 00:44:09.730
Everyday it becomes
harder and harder to live,

00:44:12.768 --> 00:44:14.403
to eat, to sleep.

00:44:18.157 --> 00:44:20.983
I have no idea how do
I live in this country.

00:44:32.627 --> 00:44:37.627
Some days I wish I just go
to live on the moon alone.

00:44:41.390 --> 00:44:46.390
But I was trying to stay
strong, if I am depressed

00:44:49.039 --> 00:44:52.300
and just think about I'm okay.

00:44:52.300 --> 00:44:53.750
I must stay alive.

00:44:53.750 --> 00:44:55.420
At least I must not die.

00:44:55.420 --> 00:44:57.123
I must not get hurt.

00:45:00.094 --> 00:45:02.333
I am trying to motivate my mind with that.

00:45:09.200 --> 00:45:12.140
- Okay, sorry, stop sharing my screen.

00:45:12.140 --> 00:45:15.480
And so it was not very
organized as a presentation,

00:45:15.480 --> 00:45:18.010
but you can ask us anything

00:45:18.010 --> 00:45:23.010
and just to finish why we have our ideas

00:45:23.330 --> 00:45:27.180
to have Thailand and Burmese
young journalists work together

00:45:27.180 --> 00:45:30.040
because obviously they face
some of the same issues

00:45:30.040 --> 00:45:33.887
in the generation and it's about politics,

00:45:33.887 --> 00:45:35.870
but it's also about the Mekong River.

00:45:35.870 --> 00:45:38.170
It's so many things
that people are sharing

00:45:38.170 --> 00:45:40.109
and have to learn about each other

00:45:40.109 --> 00:45:43.407
and the countries and the
similarities in the methods

00:45:43.407 --> 00:45:45.998
of the leaders and the colonies

00:45:45.998 --> 00:45:49.060
and there is so much people
can learn from each other.

00:45:49.060 --> 00:45:50.940
So we also organize workshop

00:45:50.940 --> 00:45:52.487
where people can share the,

00:45:54.249 --> 00:45:56.360
Thai and Burmese journalists
can share the experience

00:45:56.360 --> 00:45:58.180
of covering protest of relationship

00:45:58.180 --> 00:46:01.150
with state authorities of prison life

00:46:01.150 --> 00:46:06.150
of environmental struggle
and how trying to stay safe

00:46:06.200 --> 00:46:11.200
and how trying to do
work that will be seen

00:46:11.570 --> 00:46:14.690
because we have also this
problem that Southeast Asia

00:46:15.600 --> 00:46:19.249
has gone a bit in a whole of interest.

00:46:19.249 --> 00:46:22.480
And there was some
interest for some months

00:46:22.480 --> 00:46:27.480
in the beginning, but then
since the war in Ukraine,

00:46:28.430 --> 00:46:31.750
it's very difficult to get
people interested in Myanmar.

00:46:31.750 --> 00:46:36.750
And this is also why we, which
way to expand our articles.

00:46:37.990 --> 00:46:40.920
We can explore our website.

00:46:40.920 --> 00:46:43.270
We have articles twice a month

00:46:43.270 --> 00:46:45.820
about what we think is the main event.

00:46:45.820 --> 00:46:50.303
And actually five days after
the invasion of Ukraine,

00:46:50.303 --> 00:46:54.240
Kenyan people went protesting
from the Russian embassy

00:46:54.240 --> 00:46:56.650
in Bangkok, and some
Thai people were there

00:46:56.650 --> 00:46:58.010
and some Burmese people were there.

00:46:58.010 --> 00:47:00.693
So it was pretty incredible to see this,

00:47:01.620 --> 00:47:03.967
even not original solidarity

00:47:03.967 --> 00:47:08.290
and people could see the
same enemy in the eyes

00:47:08.290 --> 00:47:12.210
and make connection with business

00:47:12.210 --> 00:47:14.390
and military power and interest them.

00:47:14.390 --> 00:47:16.410
So we write about this too.

00:47:16.410 --> 00:47:20.430
How the situation in
Myanmar is not isolated

00:47:21.720 --> 00:47:25.870
and that it says a lot to
what's happening in the world.

00:47:25.870 --> 00:47:30.870
And of course, Myanmar was
such a hope for a lot of us.

00:47:32.105 --> 00:47:33.320
And if Myanmar fall,

00:47:33.320 --> 00:47:38.320
you have a feeling that it's a
bad trend for Southeast Asia,

00:47:39.390 --> 00:47:42.070
because they were showing
something else, very imperfect,

00:47:42.070 --> 00:47:43.455
but it was something else.

00:47:43.455 --> 00:47:44.830
There was something else.

00:47:44.830 --> 00:47:48.530
And so we tried to explain
that supporting Myanmar

00:47:48.530 --> 00:47:51.423
is supporting an idea in
Asia, but also beyond that.

00:47:52.360 --> 00:47:56.660
So you can ask any question
you want to my colleagues

00:47:56.660 --> 00:47:57.850
who also on the ground.

00:47:57.850 --> 00:48:00.973
And of course, to Miko,
we did a incredible work

00:48:00.973 --> 00:48:03.150
half of the work collective.

00:48:03.150 --> 00:48:05.983
And so thank you and
sorry for the time, yeah.

00:48:06.830 --> 00:48:07.780
- Thank you, Laure.

00:48:09.530 --> 00:48:12.323
So at this point, we will
have an open discussion.

00:48:13.430 --> 00:48:16.303
Thank you so much for both
of these presentations.

00:48:17.210 --> 00:48:22.040
I invite people to raise their
hand using the chat feature

00:48:22.040 --> 00:48:24.410
or the reaction feature on Zoom.

00:48:24.410 --> 00:48:25.720
And when the hand goes up,

00:48:25.720 --> 00:48:27.440
I'll invite you to ask the question

00:48:27.440 --> 00:48:29.483
and I'll keep track of a queue.

00:48:37.140 --> 00:48:41.280
Maybe I'll start off with a
question for Phuong Anh and Tam

00:48:43.953 --> 00:48:46.430
and maybe it's a mildly
sensitive question.

00:48:46.430 --> 00:48:49.000
And so you don't have
to answer it completely

00:48:49.000 --> 00:48:49.930
if you don't want to,

00:48:49.930 --> 00:48:54.930
but your students at Fulbright University

00:48:55.100 --> 00:48:58.890
and you're working on a topic
that raises certain questions

00:48:58.890 --> 00:49:02.053
about what's happening in Myanmar,

00:49:05.270 --> 00:49:08.790
I'm curious how you feel
about the sensitivity

00:49:08.790 --> 00:49:11.560
of raising these topics
within Vietnam itself.

00:49:11.560 --> 00:49:14.310
Obviously you're not talking
about the politics of Vietnam

00:49:14.310 --> 00:49:16.130
in a particular way,

00:49:16.130 --> 00:49:18.960
but you are talking about
another country a Zine right?

00:49:18.960 --> 00:49:23.780
And Vietnam itself has
certain obligations to a Zine,

00:49:23.780 --> 00:49:25.650
but a Zine has proven itself

00:49:25.650 --> 00:49:30.650
to be very unable to stand
up and make any claims.

00:49:31.500 --> 00:49:34.200
And so how do you navigate that situation

00:49:34.200 --> 00:49:38.150
as young Vietnamese students
who are seeing this tragedy,

00:49:38.150 --> 00:49:41.833
but also being mindful
of your own position?

00:49:44.110 --> 00:49:46.930
- So I think I would
like to take the question

00:49:46.930 --> 00:49:48.500
and if Phuong Anh have anything to add on,

00:49:48.500 --> 00:49:50.520
feel free to chime in,

00:49:50.520 --> 00:49:55.520
but you're right, Eric,
that exactly the first thing

00:49:55.610 --> 00:49:56.930
that we have to think about

00:49:56.930 --> 00:50:01.650
when even before we start to
have any tangible outcomes

00:50:01.650 --> 00:50:05.380
of the project, because
we are fully aware that.

00:50:05.380 --> 00:50:07.390
So apart from the thing
that you said about Vietnam

00:50:07.390 --> 00:50:09.860
being attached to like
the non intervention,

00:50:09.860 --> 00:50:14.660
kind of like mandate between
South Asian countries

00:50:14.660 --> 00:50:18.200
at the same time, when
we talked about events

00:50:18.200 --> 00:50:21.700
and information that concerns keywords

00:50:21.700 --> 00:50:25.067
such as rebellion, revolution,

00:50:25.067 --> 00:50:30.067
and to resist against a certain
sort of unite government.

00:50:33.420 --> 00:50:36.490
So those are some of the things

00:50:36.490 --> 00:50:40.750
that we will have to communicate
very, very carefully,

00:50:40.750 --> 00:50:42.380
even though that our main goal

00:50:42.380 --> 00:50:45.991
is to still bring out the rawest

00:50:45.991 --> 00:50:49.710
and the most kind of a
genuine kind of a perspective

00:50:49.710 --> 00:50:50.930
within the Zine.

00:50:50.930 --> 00:50:54.172
So in the beginning we intended

00:50:54.172 --> 00:50:58.350
to make it a physical kind of publication.

00:50:58.350 --> 00:51:03.350
So we would have the hard
copies for people to get

00:51:03.860 --> 00:51:07.280
and hold in their hands and get them like,

00:51:07.280 --> 00:51:08.540
if they're interested in.

00:51:08.540 --> 00:51:13.050
But a lot of that has
been probably left aside

00:51:13.050 --> 00:51:14.030
because of the communications,

00:51:14.030 --> 00:51:16.040
when it comes to print publications,

00:51:16.040 --> 00:51:18.480
and especially under
the context of Vietnam,

00:51:18.480 --> 00:51:23.480
those are one of the things
that are considered to be taboo

00:51:23.570 --> 00:51:27.016
and taken into considerations
of the content itself.

00:51:27.016 --> 00:51:30.380
So eventually, so we also
intended to have like,

00:51:30.380 --> 00:51:33.330
a Vietnamese version,
an international version

00:51:33.330 --> 00:51:35.270
where everything would be in English.

00:51:35.270 --> 00:51:40.270
So we also went through a lot
of like stages of consulting

00:51:41.960 --> 00:51:45.230
with different people who
have experienced working

00:51:45.230 --> 00:51:47.170
in independent publication.

00:51:47.170 --> 00:51:49.521
We call ourselves independent publication.

00:51:49.521 --> 00:51:52.690
And even though we are
receiving help from organization

00:51:52.690 --> 00:51:54.283
and you know, like affiliated organization

00:51:54.283 --> 00:51:56.620
that we presented in the beginning,

00:51:56.620 --> 00:52:00.230
but we're still a student
led kind of a project

00:52:00.230 --> 00:52:02.710
and we're providing our own narrative

00:52:02.710 --> 00:52:05.110
based on the materials
that we've collected.

00:52:05.110 --> 00:52:09.810
So a lot of that would not guarantee us

00:52:09.810 --> 00:52:14.250
like a certain neutrality
or a certain discourse

00:52:14.250 --> 00:52:16.800
where we would not be touched

00:52:16.800 --> 00:52:21.800
by forces that like unwanted forces.

00:52:22.130 --> 00:52:25.850
So eventually we decided to
make the Zine talent English,

00:52:25.850 --> 00:52:29.560
first of all, to like
to make the narrative

00:52:29.560 --> 00:52:32.340
a little more audible among
the international community

00:52:32.340 --> 00:52:36.080
and not limited within
the Vietnamese community.

00:52:36.080 --> 00:52:40.400
And we are participated
in this project as people.

00:52:40.400 --> 00:52:45.400
So we don't really identify
with our own national,

00:52:47.000 --> 00:52:49.740
you know, like attribution,
but rather a group of people

00:52:49.740 --> 00:52:54.080
who are, who want to pay more attention

00:52:54.080 --> 00:52:56.723
